WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.920
Speaker 1: OK, one more story having to do
with Joe Manchin killing the build back better

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.430
legislation this week.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:10.650
We have to talk about how the squad was actually
proven right and centrist Democrats were proven

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.110
wrong, at least when it comes to one important
aspect of all of this.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:20.300
A few weeks ago, when the physical infrastructure
deal was being debated, there were several

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:25.759
members of Congress, the progressive Democrats
specifically who urged House Speaker Nancy

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:31.820
Pelosi and Senate Majority Leader Chuck Schumer
to couple the infrastructure deal with the

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.820
multitrillion dollar spending bill build back
better and indeed, for a few weeks.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:41.070
Those two bills were coupled together, and
the idea was that Manchin in some of these

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:45.120
other centrist Democrats, they're sure yeses
on physical infrastructure.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.240
They definitely want to see that get passed.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.340
But when it comes to the multitrillion dollar
spending plan, we just can't trust them.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.170
They they seem to be changing their minds.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.830
And, you know, we just don't know if they're
sure yeses.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:01.230
Eventually, Nancy Pelosi decided to cave to
the moderates in the party, and they decided

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.460
to separate the two bills.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.910
And Biden gave her the stamp of approval to
do so, saying that we're going to be able

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:11.940
to assure that Joe Manchin is going to vote
yes on both pieces of legislation.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.910
So Joe Biden, he essentially gave us his word
on that.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:18.060
But the squad, they weren't buying it.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:23.200
So when it came time to actually vote on the
infrastructure deal in November, most of the

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.890
Congressional Progressive Caucus, they decided
to vote.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:31.350
Yes, that's Pramila Jayapal, Katie Porter,
Ro Khanna and a bunch of other familiar names.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:35.260
But this the six squad members, they held
firm and they voted no.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:36.530
That's Jamaal Bowman.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:37.530
Cori Bush.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:42.360
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, Ilhan Omar, Ayanna
Pressley and Rashida Tlaib.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.360
And they voted no.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.370
Not because they don't want to see infrastructure
get passed.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:47.500
That's actually quite the opposite.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.340
They definitely are in support of revamping
American infrastructure, but they viewed this

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.590
as the best bargaining chip that they had.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.960
Are making sure that both of the bills got
passed, the physical infrastructure and the

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.490
so-called human infrastructure.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:06.391
And at the time, there was a sentiment among
many Democrats that was like, Look, let's

00:02:06.391 --> 00:02:08.110
get infrastructure done.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:12.129
Biden hasn't had a significant legislative
achievement in a while, maybe not since the

00:02:12.129 --> 00:02:15.640
COVID stimulus plan was passed back in March.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.109
And we also don't know if we're going to be
able to, in the long term, maintain the 60

00:02:20.109 --> 00:02:23.330
vote threshold that we need in the Senate
to get this passed because you really can't

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.680
trust Republicans, like maybe they'll decide
they don't want to support this thing anymore.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.650
The idea was, let's get it done now.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:33.430
We'll get this round of positive press coverage
about the infrastructure deal.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:37.469
And then before the end of the year, we'll
get build back better done through budget

00:02:37.469 --> 00:02:38.469
reconciliation.

00:02:38.469 --> 00:02:43.549
And that will prompt another round of positive
media coverage and will be viewed as yet another

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:46.230
accomplishment for Joe Biden and the Democrats.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:50.549
Obviously, that didn't play out, and the squad
was right to question mansion's willingness

00:02:50.549 --> 00:02:52.650
to go along with the rest of the party.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.750
We actually have a video now of Pramila Jayapal
talking to Maggie Hassan about everything

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:02.390
that went on, and she maintains that she has
no regrets in all of this.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:04.150
But I sort of doubt that.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.690
Let's take a look at the video and then we'll
come back.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.319
Speaker 3: How do you feel about that today?

00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:09.489
Do you feel that Joe Biden let you down?

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.969
And do you feel you got played by Joe Manchin?

00:03:11.969 --> 00:03:18.299
Speaker 4: No, and no, we are, you know, for
the weeks and the days going up to the vote

00:03:18.299 --> 00:03:23.159
in the House, everybody every day, if I had
counted, I would be if I got a penny for every

00:03:23.159 --> 00:03:27.840
time somebody said to me This is not going
to happen, you all have given up everything.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.680
We got it done in the house.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:34.510
Now I am in the same place in saying that
we are getting grenades rolled off us all

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:35.510
the time.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:36.510
We have to pick them up.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:40.019
We have to put the pin back in and we have
to continue to focus on the fact that this

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.090
is going to be rocky.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:46.689
We can't hang our, you know, our commitments
and our hopes on the words of one senator

00:03:46.689 --> 00:03:48.090
or two senators.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:53.709
We have to continue to work to get it done
and the vast majority of it is done.

00:03:53.709 --> 00:04:00.239
And so I was on the phone with Senator Schumer
today with the White House, and I believe

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:01.689
we will still get it done.

00:04:01.689 --> 00:04:09.900
It's going to be rocky and we just have to
continue to leave no space in the in the commitment

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:10.900
to getting it done.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.519
And listen, the president's word is on the
line here and I do still believe that he is

00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:20.299
going to do what he told me and what he told
our caucus and what he told the country he

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:21.650
would do.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:27.680
Had we not done what we had done, though,
and if he doesn't, congresswoman.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.150
What was up?

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.100
And if he doesn't?

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.639
No, we're going to do it.

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:35.650
We're going to do it, and the leverage
Speaker 3: that you had, your critics would

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.669
argue, was lost when you voted for before.

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:42.289
I just wonder, do you regret voting for the
Biff deal now in hindsight, given it's now

00:04:42.289 --> 00:04:43.629
months later?

00:04:43.629 --> 00:04:46.860
And Joe Manchin is no closer to signing off
on a one point seventy five trillion.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.790
Speaker 4: No, I don't regret it because I
think our leverage was at the maximum point.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:55.509
Speaker 1: On the other side of the coin,
we have one of the squad members, AOC tweeting

00:04:55.509 --> 00:04:59.949
about this, saying quote when a handful of
us in the House warned this would happen if

00:04:59.949 --> 00:05:02.710
Democratic leaders gave Manchin everything
he wanted.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.270
First, by moving bef, that's the bipartisan
infrastructure framework before build back

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.620
better instead of passing together.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.729
Many ridiculed our position.

00:05:11.729 --> 00:05:17.229
Maybe they'll believe us next time, or maybe
people will just keep calling us naive.

00:05:17.229 --> 00:05:22.180
And unfortunately, given the Establishment
Democrats track record on all of this and

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:26.419
when it comes to them trying to listen to
progressives, it'll probably be the second

00:05:26.419 --> 00:05:31.180
one of those two options there, and they'll
probably just keep getting calls naive.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.169
But there is a counter argument to all of
this that we have to consider as well, and

00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:40.520
it is a strong one, which is that even if
the entire progressive caucus held firm and

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:44.540
they prevented the infrastructure deal from
getting passed in the House, and they made

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:49.379
sure that it was only going to happen in one
piece of legislation, the two bills had to

00:05:49.379 --> 00:05:51.800
be put together, and that was it.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.830
Are we sure that Joe Manchin would have actually
voted for it?

00:05:54.830 --> 00:06:00.060
Like, the argument is that he would write
because he supports the infrastructure deal

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:05.500
in West Virginia desperately needs new infrastructure,
but he just as easily could have done the

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:07.270
same exact thing here.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:09.330
He could have said, You know, I like some
pieces of this legislation.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:13.289
I like the infrastructure stuff, but there
are members of my party who are trying to

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:16.889
poison pill it with all of this other nonsense.

00:06:16.889 --> 00:06:22.039
And there was this opportunity to make this
bill bipartisan and the progressives are ruining

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:23.090
that opportunity.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:26.810
So I just can't support this bill in any form
that also could have happened.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.199
That also is a legitimate possibility.

00:06:29.199 --> 00:06:32.460
And then progressives, at the end of the day,
they look bad because they are the ones who

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:37.160
are blamed for not allowing infrastructure
to pass when even some centrist Republicans

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.160
are willing to do it.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.000
And you have the remainder of the Democratic
Party in support of it.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:46.889
So what we know for now is that the squad
was definitely right not to trust Joe Manchin,

00:06:46.889 --> 00:06:49.880
not to trust his word because his word means
nothing.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.330
But whether or not we actually would have
been able to get both of these things passed

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.840
by the end of the year.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:55.919
That remains uncertain.

00:06:55.919 --> 00:06:58.350
And to be honest, I guess we'll never truly
know.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:02.710
It's sort of an falsifiable in a sense, because
it really just comes down to what Joe Manchin

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.040
is thinking on any particular day.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.180
And that's unfortunately what we have to deal
with.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:11.090
So that's everything having to do with build
back better as of now.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:13.139
We're going to go to a break back after this.

